# Unreal Engine generated folders - never version these
Binaries/
DerivedDataCache/
Intermediate/
Saved/
Build/

# Visual Studio workspace files - regenerated via right-click .uproject > Generate project files
.vs/
*.sln
*.slnx
.vsconfig

# Content is excluded for now: the Content folder holds multi-GB Fab/Megascans packs that
# don't belong in a plain git repo. When project-authored assets (Blueprints, maps, data assets)
# start accumulating, set up Git LFS and start tracking Content/ selectively - the Fab packs
# themselves are always re-downloadable from the Fab library.
Content/

# Plugin build artifacts
Plugins/**/Binaries/
Plugins/**/Intermediate/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2026-07-26: project-authored Content is now tracked via Git LFS.
# Fab/Megascans packs stay excluded - they are re-downloadable from the Fab
# library and would bloat the repo (DreamscapeSeries alone is 2.2 GB).
# Content/ is still ignored by default above; these negations opt specific
# project-authored folders back in.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!Content/
Content/*
!Content/Characters/
!Content/Blueprints/
!Content/UI/
!Content/Input/
!Content/Maps/
!Content/VFX/
# 2026-08-04: BB_Human / BT_Militia / DA_Race_Human live here. Without this negation the entire
# defender AI layer was untracked and would have been lost on any clean checkout.
!Content/AI/

# 2026-08-05: the same class of bug as Content/AI above, found while pushing the ranged-combat
# work. Both of these are project-authored and neither was versioned.
#
#   Content/Python/  the editor authoring scripts (gs_build_burn_material.py builds the whole burn
#                    material stack; gs_build_aim_materials.py builds the aim arc + reticle). Plain
#                    text, no LFS. These GENERATE assets, so losing them means losing the ability to
#                    rebuild or retune what they made - strictly worse than losing an asset.
#   Content/Data/    DA_Weapon_Scout and friends. Weapon identity is a data operation in this
#                    project (design doc §5), so this folder is gameplay design, not imported art.
!Content/Python/
!Content/Data/

# 2026-08-21 (#249): the SAME class of bug a third time. Content/Audio/ held the
# three hand-authored horn SoundWaves - the only project-authored audio in the
# project - and was untracked, so a clean checkout lost them silently. It now
# also holds the whole mixer spine (sound classes, submixes, attenuation,
# concurrency, the base mix and the surface physical materials), which is
# authored configuration, not imported art. None of it is re-downloadable.
!Content/Audio/

# source FBX staging lives outside Content (auto-import fires on anything
# under Content/) and is not versioned - the clips come from Mixamo.
_MixamoStaging/

# Fab plugin copied into the project - reinstallable from Fab
Plugins/Marketplace/

# 2026-08-13 (#150): ACF's 40 author-written Claude skill packs, copied out of the
# plugin into .claude/skills by Tools/Register-ACFSkills.ps1 so sessions can see them.
# Same reasoning as Plugins/Marketplace above - it is marketplace content, and it is
# regenerable. The GENERATOR is versioned; its output is not. Re-run the script after
# an ACF update. Hand-written project skills, if any are ever added, would need a
# negation here.
.claude/skills/

# Local secrets - never commit (Anthropic API key for the content pipeline)
.env
.env.*
